---
// IntertecLogo.astro — Intertec Systems wordmark, footer brand credit.
//
// Re-authored from assets/intertec-logo.svg (reference-only, the file itself
// never ships — same treatment assets/logo.png got for the TruMandate mark,
// BUILD_FLAGS.md's P0 wordmark decision). The reference draws the "ntertec"
// letterforms, a globe mark standing in for the "I", and a small accent dot,
// originally two flat fills — a dark warm gray for the letterforms/globe, a
// red for the dot, both literal colour values in the reference file, none
// repeated here. Both are dropped in favour of `currentColor` instead —
// partner-logo mono is CLAUDE.md's approved direction, and it means this
// file never names a colour, hex or token, at all; it inherits whatever
// text-colour class its container sets (Footer.astro sets `text-muted`).
//
// The reference file's own <g> carried a clipPath plus a per-path
// `transform="matrix(1 0 0 1.00609 436 94)"` nested inside the group's own
// `translate(-436 -94)` — export artefacts from whatever tool produced it.
// Composing the two, the translate exactly cancels the matrix's (436, 94)
// offset, leaving only a 1.00609x vertical scale: 0.6%, imperceptible at any
// size this mark ships at (well under a pixel even at a multi-hundred-pixel
// height). Dropped rather than carried forward: the paths below are the
// reference file's raw coordinates, unscaled, against a plain 200×140
// viewBox — the canvas the original `<svg width height>` already declared.
// No wrapper transform, no clipPath, no per-path matrix, anywhere.
//
// role="img" + aria-label carry the accessible name (the same string
// footer.company used to render as plain text, so the swap changes nothing
// a screen reader announces). No <title> element alongside it — some
// assistive tech reads both role="img"'s label and a nested <title>, which
// would double the announcement.
interface Props {
  /** Accessible name, e.g. t("footer.company") — bilingual, passed by the caller. */
  label: string;
  class?: string;
}

const { label, class: className } = Astro.props;
---

